## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of demand paging, stack growth, and synchronization under contention in a simple OS.

## Key Concepts
- Demand paging for stack growth
- Per-page locking to avoid duplicate page allocations
- PTE updates, TLB invalidation, and wakeups under concurrency

## Code Example
```c
// Conceptual skeleton
void handle_fault(vaddr_t va) {
  lock(page_lock(va));
  if (pte_present(va)) { unlock(page_lock(va)); return; }
  frame_t f = alloc_frame();
  if (!f) {handle_out_of_memory(); unlock(page_lock(va)); return;}
  zero_fill(f);
  map(va, f, PRESENT);
  invalidate_TLB(va);
  unlock(page_lock(va));
}
```

